ttps://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-22T16:29:21-07:00","id":1554571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554554-an-old-1990s-gamer-s-opinion-on-bloodlines-2-review?p=1554566#post1554566\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You have to correct this, too. Even more than your little peccadilloes.<br /> <br /> The game was announced in 2015, Mitsoda was fired in 2020, HL was changed for TCR in 2021, TCR was formally announced in 2023, which was also the confirmation that the project was confirmed to be salvageable (the 2021 announcement included that they wouldn't reveal the new developer until they were sure things were going to get finished).<br /> <br /> So HL got more than 5 years to be kicked off, but the project took 10 years total, 4 and a half under TCR. Given all we know, I'd say 4 years is probably the most correct answer as I would ditch the HL attempt as a failure which was effectively cancelled, just keeping the name, but formally speaking, 10 years.<br /> <br /> As usual I disagree with your rating style, but that's a big me, overall this seems a good review.</div> </div> </div> </div>Corrected.<br /> <br /> I am curious what your rating style would be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr