s":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-22T19:00:33-07:00","id":1554582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554554-an-old-1990s-gamer-s-opinion-on-bloodlines-2-review?p=1554579#post1554579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How's the game in terms of horror? VtM has always been a horror game at heart, and Bloodlines 1 had some decent horror and jumpscare elements (Ocean House Hotel, the sewers, the warrens,,the Hollywood house, etc).</div> </div> </div> </div>The Phyre segments are largely lacking horror except for the mannequins, who are basically like Weeping Angels. Instead, the majority of horror scenes are done with Fabien, who is a much younger vampire and has an extended story where he's attempting to track down a Kindred serial killer.<br /> <br /> There's also a lot of horrible murders and revelations of characters throughout the game.<br /> <br /> But the Phyre segments have a lot of serial killer moments....with you in the driver's seat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-22T20:31:27-07:00","id":1554584,"title":"","content":"Great review, thanks. Glad you enjoyed it.<br /> <br /> - Saga","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1594-saga","name":"Saga","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-22T21:13:58-07:00","id":1554586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554554-an-old-1990s-gamer-s-opinion-on-bloodlines-2-review?p=1554571#post1554571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am curious what your rating style would be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Working from second-hand information I can, for now, just say I wouldn't say it's worth your money (because they're asking a lot) and probably give it 6 or 7, because those are good numbers for me for a game that's good, but not exceptional. Six is an enjoyable but forgettable game. Seven is outright a good game. Above this is only for games that somehow surprise me (or don't, but because the hype was already high).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T14:40:53-07:00","id":1554604,"title":"","content":"I decided to take a look at playthroughs of the game before deciding whenether to buy it. So while I didnt' had it directly in my hands, here's my takes:<br /> <br /> Positives<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b- the mood of vtm is present and well done. It was to be expected, the chinese room was first and foremost a company known for walking simulators, and these are all mood based. <br /> <br /> -the choice to take a clear inspiration from the dishonored franchise was a good one. It goes very well with the style of a vampire game, notably the movement mechanics are appreciable<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> -graphically, the game is pretty good<br /> <br /> -some for sound designs and music<br /> <br /> Negatives<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b- it really seems they were of two minds on what the story should be, the parts with Fabian sounds like a previous idea of the narrative, it breaks the rhythm of the game and isn't in itself good enough IMO to justify such breaks<br /> <br /> - both too far from bloodlines and too attached to it. The game would have been better if it wasn't supposed to be a following of bloodlines, it lost most of the rpg elements of it, yet you can see it tries to clutch on the nostalgia with the references in the main quest to the Ankara sarcophagus or characters like damselle. It force us to compare it to bloodlines 1, and the comparison is not in this game's favor<br /> <br /> &quot;I won't buy this shit&quot; level negatives:<br /> <br /> -the writing.<br /> <br /> No seriously, that's what I expected to be good in this game. I could have taken the lack of rpg elements or even a passable gameplay if the writing was good.<br /> <br /> The plot in itself is not bad, it's a well planned successions of betrayal, conspiracies and upcoming. When I'm talking about writing, I'm talking about dialogues. It is horrendous. Most speech that is not exposition is badly done. It is awkward at best and very cringe at most. I defy anyone to look at the videos showing the &quot;romance&quot; options scenes and not grind their teeth in unease.<br /> <br /> OK that point, while despite the bad writing, it's clear the voice actors are doing the best they can with the material they have, I can't say the same for Phyre. I have only seen a full playthrough with a male Phyre, so I dont' know the quality of the female voice acting, but for the male one at least Phyre alternate between robotic monotone speech and sentences so awkwardly spoke that I genuinely wondered (and I mean genuinely) at times if the voice wasn't done by AI.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bSo as for my ratings, I'll have two, one for the game in itself separated from comparison with it's predecessor, and one as a followup to bloodlines 1.<br /> <br /> If taken alone the game would be a 5 out of 10. There's mood, a functional storyline, good mechanics, but terrible character writings. So a medium game altogether<br /> <br /> Now, as a followup to bloodlines 1, it's a straight 2 out of 10.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T14:59:27-07:00","id":1554608,"title":"","content":"Phyre is a fantastic character and I wish I had more from her/him. They're basically a classic 1st Edition Vampire with etiquette, class, and a deep reverence for the Traditions that has been dumped among the stupidest Anarchs and snottiest (and I rarely use that word but all of the Camarilla court has put on SEVERE AIRS while not earning it) Ancilla in the Camarilla ever. Phyre's whole story is basically, &quot;I am surrounded by children. Stupid Children.&quot;<br /> <br /> Phyre: [to Patience] I am interested in you.<br /> Patience: Oh, you mean you want to bang? <hr /> Benny: [threatens you] Get the fuck out of my city. You have one day.<br /> Phyre: I am 400 years old and way older generation than you, dipshit. Bring it. <hr /> Ryong: A new Prince cannot stand for such an insult.<br /> Phyre: [desperately tries not to tell her to fuck off] <hr /> Fabien: It's like a grammophone but better sound quality.<br /> Phyre: I know what a record player is. (okay, that one I just wish had been an option)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-23-2025, 06:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T15:19:52-07:00","id":1554612,"title":"","content":"Eeeeh, just so I'm sure, among your exemples of why you think phyre is a great character is something you *wish* was an option, one of the bad romance options and a supposition of what he character is feeling after a comment from Ryong? <br /> <br /> There's a difference between what the character is and what you internally roleplay the character as. <br /> <br /> I mean, there's no class or etiquette with calling someone dipshit, that'd be on the contrary the behavior of one the crass newly empraced quasi anarchs of 1st edition. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T15:27:46-07:00","id":1554614,"title":"","content":"I've been playing it for a couple hours now and maybe I'll be able to finish it this weekend. But the thing that really sticks in my craw about this game is that Phyre is badly written and badly performed. There are glimpses of good voice-acting in a moment here and there (especially the Clan-specific answers go well) that make me think the voice-actor got bad direction. But... I never feel like they're a character who woke up from Torpor after a hundred years. Rather, they're a tabula rasa character with pretty much next to nothing to say about anything except &quot;I'm an Elder vampire&quot; or when you get a short reminder of somebody referencing &quot;Hey, remember when you picked that one thing about your character a while ago?&quot;. Also, considering how old Fabien is, I wish there were even more distance between Phyre and Fabien. Because if Phyre went into Torpor over a hundred years ago (and the game takes place sometime in 2024, I guess), then there are plenty of other characters around who were also around at the start of the 20th century. Or really, what I want more of is a back and forth between Phyre and Fabien where the former is someone familiar with the 19th century and Fabien someone familiar with the 21st century. Instead, so far, it's just Fabien explaining stuff to Phyre like they're a toddler. <br /> <br /> Also, the &quot;Phyre&quot;-name still feels incredibly stupid. Why not go just with &quot;Nomad&quot;? I get the part where the Elder doesn't want to reveal their real name but why Phyre? Like, seriously, the game wants us to believe that somebody asks &quot;What should I call you?&quot; and then this Elder frantically looked around, their eyes hit upon a band-poster and just decided &quot;Let's go with that.&quot;. Nomad would've been a perfectly fine alias.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T16:10:28-07:00","id":1554619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyremne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554554-an-old-1990s-gamer-s-opinion-on-bloodlines-2-review?p=1554612#post1554612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eeeeh, just so I'm sure, among your exemples of why you think phyre is a great character is something you *wish* was an option, one of the bad romance options and a supposition of what he character is feeling after a comment from Ryong</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not trying to persuade you of anything. Just sharing my enjoyment of the mood that I felt the game invoked.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've been playing it for a couple hours now and maybe I'll be able to finish it this weekend. But the thing that really sticks in my craw about this game is that Phyre is badly written and badly performed. There are glimpses of good voice-acting in a moment here and there (especially the Clan-specific answers go well) that make me think the voice-actor got bad direction. But... I never feel like they're a character who woke up from Torpor after a hundred years. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I get a detached stoic immortal not badly performed at all. They're not supposed to be natural or human.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, the &quot;Phyre&quot;-name still feels incredibly stupid. Why not go just with &quot;Nomad&quot;? I get the part where the Elder doesn't want to reveal their real name but why Phyre? Like, seriously, the game wants us to believe that somebody asks &quot;What should I call you?&quot; and then this Elder frantically looked around, their eyes hit upon a band-poster and just decided &quot;Let's go with that.&quot;. Nomad would've been a perfectly fine alias. </div> </div> </div>Yes, but it also is their alias.<br /> <br /> They're trying to keep a low profile but Safia blows that out of the water.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-23-2025, 07:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T16:31:43-07:00","id":1554621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554554-an-old-1990s-gamer-s-opinion-on-bloodlines-2-review?p=1554619#post1554619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I get a detached stoic immortal not badly performed at all. They're not supposed to be natural or human.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;detached stoic immortal&quot;... Yep, good description for a poorly written character. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554554-an-old-1990s-gamer-s-opinion-on-bloodlines-2-review?p=1554619#post1554619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but it also is their alias.<br /> <br /> They're trying to keep a low profile but Safia blows that out of the water.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nomad is an alias! The character already has an alias. <br /> <br /> And Lou Graham figures out who you are even before Safia enters the picture. <br /> <br /> Also, Phyre is a bad alias. Another bit of bad writing. You really think that a believable alias for a vampire that has been in Torpor for the last hundred years would be &quot;Fire&quot; - except it's &quot;Fire&quot; with a &quot;Ph&quot; and a &quot;Y&quot;? Come on, that's stupid! The only believable reaction to &quot;Phyre&quot; is &quot;Yeah sure... (character rolls eyes)&quot;. Hang on, the other believable reaction is &quot;Phyre...? You mean like the band?&quot;. Why even bother with this? Unless the game is trying to make fun of the protagonist, I don't see any point in doing this. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T17:56:14-07:00","id":1554625,"title":"","content":"Generally, I rate five to six as &quot;barely worth my time&quot; and only the barest minimum of enjoyment while this is much more a consistently fun experience and thus a 7-8.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-23-2025, 10:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T19:03:05-07:00","id":1554627,"title":"","content":"I don't particularly care about the alias Phyre. It's stupid, which somehow detracts from the mood of the game, but nothing that terrible.<br /> <br /> Sure, I don't think you should spin it as a good decision, either. We can argue all day and night it it's likely that an Elder would chose this stupid alias, and there's no definitive answer, but the reality is that:<br /> <br /> This is a piece of media. Everything in it has, first and foremost, a storytelling purpose. <i>As a piece of storytelling</i> Phyre is a bad name. It detracts from the mood without giving anything in return. It has some potential for humor, but if the game doesn't use this potential (which is hard to do in a horror game, but not impossible), then it has no reason to be there.<br /> <br /> Maybe it could be a sign of Phyre's personality. But as far as I can see, it isn't. It's just random (Doylist random, Whatsonian random isn't important).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-23T19:09:23-07:00","id":1554628,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554554-an-old-1990s-gamer-s-opinion-on-bloodlines-2-review?p=1554621#post1554621\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;detached stoic immortal&quot;... Yep, good description for a poorly written character.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or a vampire.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, Phyre is a bad alias. Another bit of bad writing. You really think that a believable alias for a vampire that has been in Torpor for the last hundred years would be &quot;Fire&quot; - except it's &quot;Fire&quot; with a &quot;Ph&quot; and a &quot;Y&quot;? Come on, that's stupid! The only believable reaction to &quot;Phyre&quot; is &quot;Yeah sure... (character rolls eyes)&quot;. Hang on, the other believable reaction is &quot;Phyre...? You mean like the band?&quot;. Why even bother with this? Unless the game is trying to make fun of the protagonist, I don't see any point in doing this. </div> </div> </div>I mean English would literally have changed multiple times from the time they were Embraced to the present.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-24T05:00:06-07:00","id":1554637,"title":"","content":"Considering how much a glass half full person you are Phipps, this does not bode well..<br /> <br /> As a brit im hard wired to find fault so....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-24T07:28:46-07:00","id":1554639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554554-an-old-1990s-gamer-s-opinion-on-bloodlines-2-review?p=1554637#post1554637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering how much a glass half full person you are Phipps, this does not bode well..<br /> <br /> As a brit im hard wired to find fault so....</div> </div> </div> </div>I used to be a glass half full person and then I was broken by my torture at the hands of the Tzimisce. But yes, I've been trying to be more even handed and less overtly positive in my reviews.<br /> <br /> I will say that the game is a slow burn. The absolute best parts of the game are the back half when <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">the Sabbat show up and the violence and darkness increases ten fold.</div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Ironically, I thought the Fabien parts would be my favorite of the game but I'm actually rather annoyed we can't switch back to Phyre.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-24T12:57:10-07:00","id":1554646,"title":"","content":"The thing I'm just thinking of is my experience with great games. Sure, not every game can be like that. But I think it's important to understand what a great game is like. That you take a great game and hope that this is the standard to go by, rather than looking at it like an exotic mutation. For example, the way Disco Elysium opens. That game's captivating within minutes. When you see all these effective/compelling ways of storytelling in games, it's hard to come to a game like Bloodlines 2 and be impressed. It's not that the Fabien/Phyre-stuff is inherently bad. It's just that the portrayal within the game leaves a lot to be desired so far for me. <br /> <br /> I haven't yet finished the game but I already felt a little bit alarmed when that first Fabien segment happened. Because you delve into Fabien's past and it's interesting because it relates to Phyre's present for some mysterious reason. At the beginning, I was like &quot;Okay, interesting, let's see where this goes.&quot; but then Fabien uses a power and you're getting a flashback. So, you're already in a flashback-sequence of what Fabien remembers and within that sequence, Fabien uses a power... to do a flashback. I mean, come on... doing a flashback during a flashback? Honestly, that just reinforces my feeling that this game should've been about Fabien. <br /> <br /> And Phyre... maybe I will have a different take once I finish the game. But it just feels to me like this is a character who's a victim of bad writing. Bloodlines 2 isn't an RPG. That's obvious. And even if they wanted to, TCR had neither the budget nor the time to turn it into one, apparently. I don't even want to imagine what this game looked like a year ago. And that it looks like this now shows that the developers put in some hard work over the last year for this project. But I wish the two voice-actors for Phyre would give Clan-flavored (depending on what you choose) responses for all (or at least most) of the things Phyre says. But that would cost time and (most importantly) money, of course, to make that happen. Phyre needs to talk a lot more. Often it's more &quot;Fabien talking <i>at </i>Phyre&quot; than &quot;Fabien talking <i>with </i>Phyre&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-24T13:30:52-07:00","id":1554649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554554-an-old-1990s-gamer-s-opinion-on-bloodlines-2-review?p=1554646#post1554646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing I'm just thinking of is my experience with great games. Sure, not every game can be like that. But I think it's important to understand what a great game is like. That you take a great game and hope that this is the standard to go by, rather than looking at it like an exotic mutation. For example, the way Disco Elysium opens. That game's captivating within minutes. When you see all these effective/compelling ways of storytelling in games, it's hard to come to a game like Bloodlines 2 and be impressed. It's not that the Fabien/Phyre-stuff is inherently bad. It's just that the portrayal within the game leaves a lot to be desired so far for me.<br /> <br /> I haven't yet finished the game but I already felt a little bit alarmed when that first Fabien segment happened. Because you delve into Fabien's past and it's interesting because it relates to Phyre's present for some mysterious reason. At the beginning, I was like &quot;Okay, interesting, let's see where this goes.&quot; but then Fabien uses a power and you're getting a flashback. So, you're already in a flashback-sequence of what Fabien remembers and within that sequence, Fabien uses a power... to do a flashback. I mean, come on... doing a flashback during a flashback? Honestly, that just reinforces my feeling that this game should've been about Fabien.<br /> <br /> And Phyre... maybe I will have a different take once I finish the game. But it just feels to me like this is a character who's a victim of bad writing. Bloodlines 2 isn't an RPG. That's obvious. And even if they wanted to, TCR had neither the budget nor the time to turn it into one, apparently. I don't even want to imagine what this game looked like a year ago. And that it looks like this now shows that the developers put in some hard work over the last year for this project. But I wish the two voice-actors for Phyre would give Clan-flavored (depending on what you choose) responses for all (or at least most) of the things Phyre says. But that would cost time and (most importantly) money, of course, to make that happen. Phyre needs to talk a lot more. Often it's more &quot;Fabien talking <i>at </i>Phyre&quot; than &quot;Fabien talking <i>with </i>Phyre&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>For me, I define a roleplaying game as the ability to decide how your character reacts and makes decisions based on their personality and how you define them.<br /> <br /> You can judge Phyre's backstory, his Clan, and how interactions that determine your ending.<br /> <br /> It's a Roleplaying Game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-24T13:53:50-07:00","id":1554650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554554-an-old-1990s-gamer-s-opinion-on-bloodlines-2-review?p=1554649#post1554649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For me, I define a roleplaying game as the ability to decide how your character reacts and makes decisions based on their personality and how you define them.<br /> <br /> You can judge Phyre's backstory, his Clan, and how interactions that determine your ending.<br /> <br /> It's a Roleplaying Game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhm, absolutely not. <i>It has to happen within the game to count as a roleplaying game</i>. Leveling up characters, choices within the story leading to different outcomes. At upper limit, you get something like Baldurs Gate 3 and of course not every RPG has to go that hard when it comes to RPG-elements. But for example, skill-checks to unlock doors, dialogue-options or specific actions within the environment. Or combat-encounters that can be ignored because you can sneak through vents or passages. Or you can neutralize bosses through doing sidequests. Stuff like that. The point of a roleplaying-<i>videogame </i>is to offer a lot of options to deal with challenges. And the more free space the game offers with these options, the better it is at facilitating a roleplaying-experience. And that includes endings and hopefully multiple endings for various NPCs. Now, every game is of course limited by its budget and allowed development-time, so the scope for these things obviously isn't endless and it rarely is something on the level of a Baldurs Gate 3.<br /> <br /> But with Bloodlines 2, it's easy... It's not an RPG. You have your linear narrative. There's a barebones skill-system that only affects combat. And then there's the dialogue-stuff related to the narrative - which has nothing to do with roleplaying. It's just a couple options and as far as the game is concerned, it's just &quot;Option 1: Average answer Option 2: Bad answer Option 3: Good answer&quot;. So the challenge there is your standard dialogue-puzzle of &quot;What is the right thing for Phyre to say in this moment?&quot;. That has nothing to do with roleplaying. That there isn't more to it is lamentable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-24T14:15:36-07:00","id":1554651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554554-an-old-1990s-gamer-s-opinion-on-bloodlines-2-review?p=1554650#post1554650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Uhm, absolutely not. <i>It has to happen within the game to count as a roleplaying game</i>. Leveling up characters, choices within the story leading to different outcomes. At upper limit, you get something like Baldurs Gate 3 and of course not every RPG has to go that hard when it comes to RPG-elements. But for example, skill-checks to unlock doors, dialogue-options or specific actions within the environment. Or combat-encounters that can be ignored because you can sneak through vents or passages. Or you can neutralize bosses through doing sidequests. Stuff like that. The point of a roleplaying-<i>videogame </i>is to offer a lot of options to deal with challenges. And the more free space the game offers with these options, the better it is at facilitating a roleplaying-experience. And that includes endings and hopefully multiple endings for various NPCs. Now, every game is of course limited by its budget and allowed development-time, so the scope for these things obviously isn't endless and it rarely is something on the level of a Baldurs Gate 3.<br /> <br /> But with Bloodlines 2, it's easy... It's not an RPG. You have your linear narrative. There's a barebones skill-system that only affects combat. And then there's the dialogue-stuff related to the narrative - which has nothing to do with roleplaying. It's just a couple options and as far as the game is concerned, it's just &quot;Option 1: Average answer Option 2: Bad answer Option 3: Good answer&quot;. So the challenge there is your standard dialogue-puzzle of &quot;What is the right thing for Phyre to say in this moment?&quot;. That has nothing to do with roleplaying. That there isn't more to it is lamentable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rules to me have nothing to do with Roleplaying Games. It's about whether you can create the role and embodty it beyond a set character and affect the story.<br /> <br /> Bluntly, lockpicking is something you can do in any game with a set protagonist and story.<br /> <br /> YMMV but that's how I define a roleplaying game. <br /> <br /> You play a role you create.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-24T14:42:10-07:00","id":1554652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554554-an-old-1990s-gamer-s-opinion-on-bloodlines-2-review?p=1554651#post1554651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rules to me have nothing to do with Roleplaying Games. It's about whether you can create the role and embodty it beyond a set character and affect the story.<br /> <br /> Bluntly, lockpicking is something you can do in any game with a set protagonist and story.<br /> <br /> YMMV but that's how I define a roleplaying game.<br /> <br /> You play a role you create.</div> </div> </div> </div>We're talking about videogames. And a specific genre of video games. I have mentioned specfic games. But your stance sounds like &quot;If there's a moment where two people touch in a novel, that's romance. YMMV but that's how I define romance-stories.&quot; I mean, it's hard to argue with you when your proposed beliefs are this flimsy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27535-knightingale","name":"Knightingale","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27535_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-24T20:30:23-07:00","id":1554654,"title":"","content":"My own review:<br /> Not that I doubt anyone cares much.<br /> <br /> My brother picked the game up and I've been watching him play it and playing a bit over at his place. It's definitely pretty mid. The Fabian sections are extremely bad. There's some potential there, but they keep having you swap to Fabian at really bad times. Further, Fabian has no travel skills so you have to walk from one of the map to the other in order to talk to someone and then walk back again and repeat this process until you finally get to swap back to Phyre. Even on the first playthru these sections are kind of a slog. I can't imagine ever replaying this game without a &quot;Remove Fabian&quot; mod. I think the game would have been much better if they had changed the Fabian sections to more of a visual novel setup, or something because they are not fun.<br /> <br /> I also found that the devs want you to play their way, not your way. For example, if there's a building they want you to go in, you have to go in the way they want. Like, let's say it's a warehouse and you don't want to go through the front entrance and fight a million goons. Tough luck, because that's the only entrance. There's no side doors or entrances, and if you climb up on the roof, there's no other entrance up, no rooftop windows or anything, so you have to go back down and walk through the front door.<br /> <br /> But wait!<br /> <br /> Once you try to walk through the front door, you get a message that instead, you need sneak in through the rooftop. How? There was no door on the rooftop! You just checked! But once you go up there, now suddenly there's a door there. That door wasn't there earlier, it was programmed to only appear after you try and go through the front door. So the game is completely on the rails.<br /> <br /> This was pretty disappointing. There's a lot of games that allow you multiple methods for solving problems. Like even in the original Bloodlines, just the house on Santa Monica beach with the thugs had several ways you could get inside, and several ways to complete the mission (kill everyone, sneak inside, blow up the power generator to get everyone to come outside, etc). With Bloodlines 2, there's basically no thinking or coming up with strategies that works for the player. TCR has one way to play the game, and you will play the game that way.<br /> <br /> The voice acting is hit or miss. There's some good and some bad. The combat is okay. It's not bad enough to detract from the game, but it's also not fun enough for me to want the combat sections to last longer. I feel like you actually top out on your powers a bit too quickly, and once you do leveling feels kind of pointless.<br /> <br /> You only have room on your power tray for a couple of powers, so getting a new power means you have to replace one of your old powers. I wish they had included an option to have multiple power trays so you could quickly swap between three or four different sets of powers. That would make leveling and learning new abilities feel more rewarding. Hopefully someone can make a mod allowing for quickswapping between powersets, I think that would really help make the combat more fun and leveling feel more rewarding.<br /> <br /> The lack of a manual save was definitely a choice. I imagine they didn't want to include one to push people to replay the game so that they can see the choices they missed the first time, but the game just doesn't feel worth replaying (especially due to Fabian), so after I've finished I'll just look at different endings on Youtube.<br /> <br /> Overall it feels like a solid 6/10 game. It's not particularly bad (other than what a slog the Fabian sections are) but it doesn't feel like it does anything particularly well. As a comparison I felt that Swansong was a 6.5. Bloodlines 2 definitely feels more polished than Swansong, and graphically it's really nice, but at the same time I think the core game underneath Swansong was better, and I'd probably recommend it over Bloodlines 2 to people looking for a VtM game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 10-24-2025, 11:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-24T20:55:50-07:00","id":1554655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554554-an-old-1990s-gamer-s-opinion-on-bloodlines-2-review?p=1554646#post1554646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing I'm just thinking of is my experience with great games. Sure, not every game can be like that. But I think it's important to understand what a great game is like. That you take a great game and hope that this is the standard to go by, rather than looking at it like an exotic mutation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's a bit extreme. It's certainly fair to expect a great game to set new market standards, but it isn't to expect every game to follow so close.<br /> <br /> Most games will be mediocre, and that's not necessarily a bad thing. Not an 8/10 thing, but not a bad thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">doing a flashback during a flashback?</div> </div> </div> </div>Frankenstein relates the tale of the journey of Robert to the Arctic Circle. It then has, at a certain point, Robert relating his conversation with Victor, in which Victor tells the bulk of the story. A big part of it is Victor relating his conversation with the Creature, in which the Creature tells his own, lengthy story. And then there's a moment when the Creature relates his conversation with the old man in the cottage, in which the old man tells the story of the family, including recent events.<br /> <br /> I don't think this gimmick is a problem, regardless if Fabien's a better character or even protagonist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knightingale</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Phyre...</div> </div> </div> </div>I can't say for sure since I didn't played the game myself, but it seems Phyre was plagued by being last priority in a very hard place. Time constraints, budget constraints, the many needs of their writing since it would be central to many things within the story. And Paradox had already spent the bulk of their resources and patience with HL's failure.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554554-an-old-1990s-gamer-s-opinion-on-bloodlines-2-review?p=1554649#post1554649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For me, I define a roleplaying game as the ability to decide how your character reacts and makes decisions based on their personality and how you define them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's not how you define RPG as a video-game genre.<br /> <br /> Video-Games are interactive media. Interactivity is already part and parcel of how any storytelling in it works. Anything you do in a video-game is by definition the character reacting and making decisions. And it isn't based on their personality, also by definition, because decisions based on the character's personality happen within the fiction, not the interactivity. When it comes to your decision, you do it as you wish, and how you perceive the character is relevant only as far as you want it to.<br /> <br /> Giving options that take into consideration earlier choices is nice, as is having this affect the fiction being told, but those aren't genre-specific mechanics in a video-game.<br /> <br /> What defines RPG as a video-game genre is the presence of classic TTRPG-adjacent mechanics and their centrality to the game-play. <i>Bloodlines</i> was an RPG because it literally gave you a complex character sheet to fill that would affect a lot of options and results during the game, and you would improve it with XP. There are other possibilities, but the point is that this was central to the game's mechanics, it wasn't just a limited set of powers that didn't really cover most of the action.<br /> <br /> <i>Bloodlines 2</i> is not an RPG. And that's not a problem, by any means (except in the <i>proper sequel</i> discussion). It doesn't make it less a story-driven game. It just defines its genre as a game.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-25T16:57:07-07:00","id":1554674,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1554554-an-old-1990s-gamer-s-opinion-on-bloodlines-2-review?p=1554651#post1554651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Rules to me have nothing to do with Roleplaying Games. It's about whether you can create the role and embody it beyond a set character and affect the story.<br /> <br /> Bluntly, lockpicking is something you can do in any game with a set protagonist and story.<br /> <br /> YMMV but that's how I define a roleplaying game.<br /> <br /> You play a role you create.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, that makes from an awfully large definition. By that logic every game where there's even just a choice of end is an RPG. Far cry 3 becomes a RPG, hell, even some call of duties becomes RPG. <br /> <br /> Plus, by that definition, bloodlines 2 is hardly an RPG. You hardly create a role for Phyre, nearly all reactions you can choose ar ee without a shred of impact on the story, the way you play is pretty much set, even with different choice of clans. In the end, the only choice that do matter is your choice of ending. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's the same problem with the tendancy to call every game whith a system of inventory/stats or a progression system an RPG. It does not approach what the concept means <br /> <br /> <br /> The concept of RPG is simple, it's about trying to match the TTRPGs from which it is born. <br /> <br /> That means mainly offering a plethora of option to match the creativity with which TTRPGs players can react to something. <br /> <br /> There should be character creation with a big impact of the creation choices, the ability to have an impact on the world, consequences for our actions. <br /> <br /> That's why people complain about lockpicking nit being present. It's not the act of lockpicking that made BL1 an rpg, it's that if you chose to invest int hat ability, you had other way to go around the game that utterly change a lot of your play than if you lacked it. <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> <br /> Bloodlines did it well. The way you chose your stats changed what you could hope to achieve in game, you could resolve a hell lot of situation with ether raw violence, sneakyness or pure dialogue. Your choice of clan changed the way npcs reacted to you. Your choices in quests made you alli\u00e9es or closed doors to you. I wasn't perfect t, thanks a hellish devellopement, but it offered what was promised. <br /> <br /> Bloodlines 2 does not offer that. The impact of our choices are minimal, you cannot get yourself permanent ennemies of, for exemple, the primo gens as you could with Strauss in BL1, you'll always end up in a mostly combat based resolution of problems. <br /> <br /> It's not an Action rpg, it's an action adventure game<br /> <br /> And that kind of thing will become more obvious as we're living Ina. Sort of renaissance of the rpg genre, and not just with baldur's gate 3.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24043-nyremne","name":"Nyremne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"414"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-25T21:21:10-07:00","id":1554679,"title":"","content":"Personally I feel like an RPG needs one of two things:<br /> <br /> 1) A robust mechanical system with stats, inventory and powers/spell mechanics. Most JRPGs fall into this one.<br /> <br /> 2) A deep system of story driven choices that allow the player to choices in how the story will play out. Something like Mass Effect 2/3 or Dragon Age 2+ fall into this one.<br /> <br /> Many classic CRPGs (Baldur's Gate, Bloodlines 1, etc) tend to comprise both of these, having fairly deep mechanical complexity as well as a lot of player driven options when it comes to seeing how the story will unfold. <br /> <br /> I feel like Bloodlines 2 does, mostly, fit into the RPG category, mainly due to the second part (I haven't finished it yet so I'm unsure how much your choices will matter), but there is also some depth with the Disciplines (there would be more if you had the option to equip more Disciplines). It's worth noting that Steam and other distributors classify Bloodlines 2 as an RPG. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov